[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[b]You need BepInEx for PEAK first:[/b] [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/peak/p/BepInEx/BepInExPack_PEAK/]BepInExPack for PEAK[/url] (5.4.75301). Without it the mod does nothing.

[b]Manual install:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInExPack for PEAK into your PEAK folder (the folder with [font=Courier New]PEAK.exe[/font]).
[*]Extract this archive into the same PEAK folder - the DLL ends up in [font=Courier New]PEAK/BepInEx/plugins/PeakWorkshop/PeakWorkshop.dll[/font].
[*]Start PEAK. The [b]Peak Workshop[/b] sign drops into the main menu.
[/list]

[b]Updating:[/b] extract the new archive over the old one. Your maps and settings stay in [font=Courier New]PEAK/BepInEx/PeakWorkshop/[/font] and are not touched.

[b]Prefer a mod manager?[/b] Peak Workshop is also on [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/peak/p/PeakCode/PeakWorkshop/]Thunderstore[/url] - with r2modman or the Thunderstore Mod Manager BepInEx comes along automatically.

[size=5][b]Requirements & compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Everyone in a lobby needs Peak Workshop.[/b] Mod lobbies are separate rooms, so friends without the mod won't see or join them.
[*]Maps, assets and items your lobby needs download automatically when you join.
[*]Peak Workshop needs an internet connection for the online Workshop and the lobby browser. Solo play and the editor work with your local content.
[*][b]Not compatible with TerrainRandomiser.[/b] It breaks the map build (maps look half-finished). Disable it while you play Peak Workshop maps.
[*]Other mods that change map generation may conflict as well. If a map looks broken, try without them first.
[*]English, German and Simplified Chinese interface (switch in the Workshop panel; “auto” follows the game language). Chinese by TFJSN (ETWML) – texts newer than its table show in English.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Online features & privacy[/b][/size]

The online Workshop and the lobby browser run on the Peak Workshop server. To use them, the mod sends:

[list]
[*]your [b]Steam ID and Steam name[/b] - to sign you in, show who uploaded content and who hosts a lobby,
[*][b]the content you publish[/b] (maps, 3D assets, items, NPC packs, thumbnails) and your ratings, subscriptions and reports,
[*][b]lobby details[/b] while you host (name, map, mode, region, player count).
[/list]

The server keeps your IP address with sign-in sessions and reports to stop spam and abuse. No passwords, no payment data, no tracking.

[b]Content rules:[/b] only upload what you made yourself or are allowed to share. Every 3D asset needs its origin and license. No hateful, sexual or illegal content. Use the [b]Report[/b] button on any Workshop page - creators see why their content was reported (never who reported it), and reported content can be hidden or removed.

[size=5][b]FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Does it change normal PEAK?[/b]
No. Host Game and Play Offline stay 100 % vanilla. The mod only kicks in when you start through the Peak Workshop sign.

[b]Do my friends need it?[/b]
Yes, everyone in the lobby needs the mod. The maps themselves download automatically.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes. Peak Workshop and everything in the Workshop are free.

[b]Where are my maps stored?[/b]
In [font=Courier New]PEAK/BepInEx/PeakWorkshop/[/font] (in your mod manager profile folder when you use one). Mod updates don't touch it.

[b]How do I report a bug or content?[/b]
[b]Content:[/b] open it in the Workshop and press [b]Report[/b]. [b]Bugs, feedback and questions:[/b] post them in the [url=https://discord.com/channels/1363179626435707082/1555303572415971388]PEAK Modding Discord (Peak Workshop thread)[/url].

[b]Why does a map take a moment to load?[/b]
Custom maps are built while you load in. Big maps can take a few seconds longer than a vanilla run - grab a snack.

[size=5][b]Known problems[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Very small 3D models (some packs are 30 cm tall) are not scaled up automatically. The upload screen points it out - use the scale slider or [b]Fit to height[/b].
[/list]

Found something else? Tell us in the [url=https://discord.com/channels/1363179626435707082/1555303572415971388]PEAK Modding Discord (Peak Workshop thread)[/url].

